-- 1908_ca_wrong_person_rows_season2.sql
-- 47 California stance rows whose evidence describes SOMEBODY ELSE, blanked in Season 2.
-- Eight people. Season 1 is CLOSED and IMMUTABLE, so a contaminated Season 1 chair is removed
-- by WRITING A SEASON 2 BLANK over it: 42 new Season 2 rows, 5 updates to rows that exist.
--
-- ══ WHAT THIS IS ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- These rows are not thinly sourced. They are AFFIRMATIVELY FALSE: each one shows a voter a
-- chair derived from a different politician's legislative record. Seven of the eight people are
-- Assembly members carrying a STATE SENATOR's record; in two cases the borrowed record also
-- inverts the member's politics (Macedo and Chen are Republicans seated on Democrats' records).
--
--   Jasmeet Kaur Bains    21 rows   ← Sen. Maria Elena Durazo   (ALL 23 of her rows are Durazo's;
--                                     21 here, immigration is blocked, 1 already at 0)
--   Alexandra M. Macedo    6 rows   ← Sen. Lena Gonzalez
--   Patrick J. Ahrens      6 rows   ← Sen. Benjamin Allen
--   Dr. Corey A. Jackson   4 rows   ← Sen. Thomas Umberg
--   James C. Ramos         4 rows   ← Sen. Sasha Renée Pérez
--   Phillip Chen           3 rows   ← Sen. Bob Archuleta
--   Gregg Hart             2 rows   ← an SD-27 senator, not identified to proof
--   Catherine Stefani      1 row    ← an SD-22 senator, not identified to proof
--
-- ══ 🔑 HOW EACH ONE IS PROVED, WITHOUT FETCHING A SINGLE PAGE ═════════════════════════════════
-- Three independent tests, used together, and every attribution rests on at least two:
--   1. THE HOUSE OF ORIGIN. In California the LEAD author of an SB sits in the Senate and of an
--      AB in the Assembly. A row crediting an Assembly member with "authoring SB 634" is
--      describing a senator. (⚠ CO-authorship crosses houses and proves nothing.)
--   2. THE BORROWED DISTRICT SITE. sd##.senate.ca.gov cited under an Assembly member is that
--      senator's own site. This is what the name-matching detectors could not see: a borrowed
--      OFFICIAL SITE scores clean on every name test.
--   3. THIS DATABASE'S OWN ROWS FOR THE REAL AUTHOR credit the same bills to them -- SB 1444 and
--      SB 867 to Benjamin Allen, SB 91 to Thomas Umberg, SB 610 and SB 634 to Sasha Renée Pérez,
--      SB 1407 to Bob Archuleta, SB 252/SB 12/SJR 2/SB 1182 to Lena Gonzalez.
-- Plus, where the row says it outright: three Bains rows name "Durazo"; three Chen rows call a
-- Republican Assembly member a "Democratic senator"; a Ramos row calls him the "youngest state
-- senator"; and Ahrens, first elected in 2024, is credited with a 2021-22 constitutional
-- amendment.
--
-- ══ ⚠ WHAT THIS MIGRATION DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO ════════════════════════════════════════════
-- It does not re-seat anybody. Removing a false chair and establishing a true one are different
-- jobs, and the second needs each member's own record read from leginfo. Re-research is owed and
-- is recorded in the pass's durable record.
-- It does not touch Season 1: those rows stay as the historical artefact they are.
-- It does not touch rows that are merely thinly sourced -- that is the separate 133-key
-- generic-profile-sourcing cohort.
--
-- ══ 🔴 EIGHT MORE ROWS ARE CONTAMINATED AND CANNOT BE FIXED ═══════════════════════════════════
-- Every one of these eight people also has a false `immigration` row, and `immigration` has NO
-- SEASON 2 PIN -- the national 1,678-stance orphan. There is no Season 2 row to write, so the
-- false Season 1 chair stays visible: Bains 1, Macedo 1, Jackson 2, Hart 2, Ramos 2, Chen 2,
-- Ortega 2, Bennett 4. That is 8 of a running national total of 146 chairs blocked on this topic.
--
-- ══ PRIOR ART ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- A pass on 2026-10-07 already caught three people in this same class and blanked 14 rows:
-- Liz Ortega (← Sen. Laura Richardson, 5), Steve Bennett (← Sen. Suzette Martinez Valladares, 4)
-- and Katy Yaroslavsky (← Supervisor Sheila Kuehl, 5). This file finishes the sweep.
--
-- No migration runner exists; this file records SQL applied by hand.


